{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Part B — durable fix (Option 1), Phase 2 for e4f3. Pushed to Gerrit as change 2454 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2454), RED->GREEN under the /rebar-debug protocol. Fresh worktree off origin/main (5c28ce66bbfd); all cmds run with the worktree venv first on PATH. NO --force anywhere.\n\nRoot cause (proven, Phase 1): mcp_retire_image (infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh) removes a compose-mcp:<sha> image ONLY at the reap of a live-tracked container; a per-release tag whose container was already reaped (or never tracked on this box) leaks forever — `docker image prune` without -a never touches a tagged image. Once the mcp blue-green family (fd4a) landed as a SECOND image family on the 30GiB root, the leak re-filled root and re-tripped rebar-root-disk-pressure, fail-closing LLM-Review. Regression of 3a52 (whose snapshot-GC watermark fix is intact — this is a NEW consumer, not a reversion).\n\nFix: new mcp_reconcile_orphans, invoked from mcp_retire_sweep (runs on BOTH the active-deploy and the no-op tick, after the reap loop). It enumerates mcp image tags newest-first and retires true orphans, PRESERVING blue-green rollback: the LIVE backend image AND the immediately-previous release (newest non-live <sha> tag) are always kept, plus the bare build tag / :latest / :prev. Removal via `docker image rm` WITHOUT -f (daemon still-referenced refusal is an independent backstop); fails SAFE (touches nothing) if the live image can't be identified.\n\nRED->GREEN evidence:\n- RED first: added test_orphaned_per_release_tags_with_no_container_are_reconciled + test_reconcile_never_retires_live_or_immediately_previous (the live+previous preservation invariant is its own test case), plus a `docker images` model + _seed_image helper in the blue-green harness. Ran before implementing -> FAILED (cmds=[]; no reconciliation existed).\n- GREEN after implementing: both new tests pass. Full related suite GREEN: tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py + test_autodeploy_disk_pressure.py + tests/unit/test_autodeploy_prune.py + test_observability_disk_pressure.py = 79 passed.\n- make lint PASS (ruff + format + shellcheck + all repo gates); make typecheck PASS (mypy, 718 files, no issues).\n\nCommit 627faccae8df: `rebar-ticket: e4f3-1661-2319-4a76` trailer + DCO Signed-off-by + Change-Id I39cdfefd; `rebar verify-commit-ticket --rev HEAD` = OK. caused_by fd4a retained.\n\nNot closing e4f3 until change 2454 is Verified +1 (per the git-workflow policy) and reclaimed root keeps LLM-Review healthy."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788145096625601268,"uuid":"e8117a33-8275-4883-a860-8fe09abdb8e7"}